---
description: Playwright QA authoring conventions
globs:
  - "**/*.spec.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

Before writing or changing Playwright tests, read:

- `core/ai/qa-principles.md`
- `core/ai/smoke-test-model.md` (smoke authoring gate)
- The `playwright-automation` skill in `.agents/skills/playwright-automation/`

Write tests against observable browser behavior. Prefer stable user-facing locators, clear setup, and targeted assertions. Assert only behavior confirmed in `.agents/qa-project-context.md`, an **approved** `scenarios/smoke-proposal.md` case, an approved scenario in `scenarios/approved/`, or an approved bug report.

Smoke: implement only SMK-* cases approved in `smoke-proposal.md`. `observation`-sourced cases need per-case approval before assertions.

Do not weaken assertions, skip tests, delete tests, or update baselines without explicit human approval.

Run the smallest relevant Playwright command before broad suites.
